@page "/demo/diagram"
@using FlexCore.Showcase.Components.Shared

@* 2026-10-25: new page on FeatureDemoLayout; two examples (booking workflow with NodeClicked, shapes/connectors/links). Facts checked
   against Diagram/DiagramControl.razor, DiagramControl.razor.css and DiagramModels.cs in FlexCore 0.2.49. The control has no layout
   engine (OffsetX/OffsetY are hand-set centres), no drag, zoom or editing, and no keyboard or ARIA support on nodes; the workflow's
   Previous/Next buttons are the page's keyboard route. Connector Ids are page-unique (wf-*, sh-*) because the arrowhead marker ids
   are document-wide. 
   2026-10-26: Previous/Next stop at the ends instead of wrapping (Next from Documents sent went to Declined, Previous from the first step too). *@

<PageTitle>Diagram — FlexCore Showcase</PageTitle>

<FeatureDemoLayout Title="Diagram" Category="Components" ControlName="DiagramControl"
                   Tagline="Boxes and arrows placed by hand and drawn as one inline SVG: six node shapes, labelled connectors and a click event."
                   SourcePath="Diagram/DiagramControl.razor;Diagram/DiagramControl.razor.css;Diagram/DiagramModels.cs">
    <Overview>
        <p>
            <code>DiagramControl</code> draws a list of <code>Nodes</code> and the <code>Connectors</code> between them as a single
            <code>&lt;svg&gt;</code>. There is no automatic layout: each node's <code>OffsetX</code> and <code>OffsetY</code> give its centre
            in pixels. A connector names two node Ids, picks a side of each node unless you set the ports, and draws a straight or right-angled
            line with an optional arrowhead and label. A click on an enabled node raises <code>NodeClicked</code> and then follows the node's
            <code>NavigateUrl</code>. The control has no dragging, zooming or editing; to change the diagram, change the node and connector
            objects and let the page re-render.
        </p>
    </Overview>

    <Examples>
        <DemoExample Id="workflow" Title="A booking workflow" RazorCode="@Code.Workflow" CSharpCode="@Code.WorkflowCs" CssCode="@Code.WorkflowCss">
            <Description><p>Showcase Travel's trip requests from first contact to travel documents. Every position is set by hand, and with the default <code>Auto</code> ports each connector leaves from the side that faces its target. Click a step, or use Previous step and Next step (they walk the main path, then the declined branch), and the panel shows who handles it and how long it usually takes; the page marks the current step with a <code>CssClass</code> styled through <code>::deep</code>.</p></Description>
            <Demo>
                <div class="wf-layout">
                    <div class="canvas">
                        <DiagramControl Nodes="_workflowNodes" Connectors="_workflowConnectors" Width="460" Height="530"
                                        Padding="12" SizePadPercent="0" NodeClicked="OnStepClicked" />
                    </div>
                    <CardControl CssClass="wf-panel" Title="@Current.Label" Subtitle="@CurrentStep.Owner" aria-live="polite">
                        <ChildContent>
                            <dl class="wf-facts">
                                <dt>Typical time</dt>
                                <dd>@CurrentStep.Typical</dd>
                                <dt>What happens</dt>
                                <dd>@CurrentStep.Detail</dd>
                            </dl>
                        </ChildContent>
                        <FooterContent>
                            <div class="wf-buttons">
                                <ButtonControl OnClick="() => Move(-1)">Previous step</ButtonControl>
                                <ButtonControl OnClick="() => Move(1)">Next step</ButtonControl>
                            </div>
                        </FooterContent>
                    </CardControl>
                </div>
            </Demo>
        </DemoExample>

        <DemoExample Id="shapes" Title="Shapes, connectors and links" RazorCode="@Code.Shapes" CSharpCode="@Code.ShapesCs">
            <Description><p>Each node's second line names its shape. <code>Rectangle</code> and <code>RoundedRectangle</code> both round their corners by <code>CornerRadius</code>, so the Rectangle here sets it to 0. "Visa needed?" forks from its bottom port: "yes" is a default orthogonal connector, "no" a <code>Straight</code> one with both ports set. The other connectors show a closed arrowhead, a dash pattern, a wider coloured line and <code>IsBroken</code>. "Package chosen" has a <code>NavigateUrl</code>; while Follow links is off, the <code>NodeClicked</code> handler sets <code>Handled</code> and the page stays put. The grey node has <code>Enabled</code> false. Hover "Package chosen" or "Departure" for their tooltips.</p></Description>
            <Demo>
                <div class="controls">
                    <SwitchControl @bind-Checked="_followLinks" Label="Follow links" />
                </div>
                <div class="canvas">
                    <DiagramControl Nodes="_shapeNodes" Connectors="_shapeConnectors" Width="550" Height="330"
                                    Padding="12" SizePadPercent="0" NodeClicked="OnShapeClicked" />
                </div>
                <p class="status" aria-live="polite">@_status</p>
            </Demo>
        </DemoExample>
    </Examples>

    <Vocabulary>
        <DocSections>
            <DocSection Id="doc-diagramcontrol-parameters" Title="DiagramControl parameters" Count='@DocSection.Label(Vocab.Params.Length, "parameters")' Open="true">
                <ApiTable Kind="ApiKind.Parameters" Title="DiagramControl parameters" Rows="Vocab.Params" />
            </DocSection>
            <DocSection Id="doc-diagramnode" Title="DiagramNode" Count='@DocSection.Label(Vocab.Node.Length, "properties")'>
